---
import InternalLayout from '@/layouts/InternalLayout.astro';
---

<InternalLayout
  title="Brand Book — Voice & Tone"
  description="PTT v3.0.0 voice in English (international) and Spanish (Colombian/LATAM)."
  section="brand"
  subsection="voice-and-tone"
>
  <main class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-8 space-y-12">
    <header class="space-y-3">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
        <a href="/internal/brand" class="hover:underline">Brand</a> / Voice &amp; Tone
      </p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Voice &amp; Tone</h1>
      <p class="text-base text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 max-w-3xl">
        Pereira Tech Talks writes the way a good mentor speaks: warm, direct,
        specific, and never patronizing. We ship in English (international) and
        Spanish (Colombian, accessible to all of LATAM). Both languages share
        the same principles, but each has its own mechanics.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Pillars</h2>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-sm">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Specific over generic</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Real numbers, real names, real outcomes. Replace adjectives with evidence.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Plural &amp; inclusive</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">"We" / "the community". Avoid framing the site as one person's project.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Plain language</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Define jargon on first use. Prefer short sentences. Cut filler words.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 p-5 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Action &amp; invitation</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Every page should leave the reader with one obvious next step.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">English (international)</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 space-y-1">
        <li>International English — avoid US-only idioms ("home run", "ballpark").</li>
        <li>Active voice. Direct addresses ("we" / "you").</li>
        <li>One exclamation mark per page max. Period.</li>
        <li>No marketing buzzwords (synergy, leverage, revolutionize, ecosystem-as-a-service).</li>
        <li>Numbers: spell out one through nine; use digits for 10+. Always digits for stats and dates.</li>
        <li>Capitalize event names ("Pereira Tech Day 2024") and proper nouns; everything else sentence-case.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">
        <table class="min-w-full text-sm">
          <thead class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800">
            <tr class="text-left">
              <th class="px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">Do</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">Don't</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-200 dark:divide-gray-700">
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">"Pereira Tech Talks runs monthly meetups in Pereira since 2017."</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">"We're a leading-edge synergistic ecosystem revolutionizing tech in the Pereira region."</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">"Become a speaker — share what you've learned."</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">"Apply now — limited spots!!!"</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">"Sponsors get logo placement, a lightning-talk slot, and a one-year partnership track."</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">"Premium tier sponsors enjoy unparalleled benefits at the best value."</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">"We met every Friday during quarantine — 130+ talks since."</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">"Join the journey of innovation that keeps redefining the limits."</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Español (regional Colombiano, accesible a LATAM)</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 space-y-1">
        <li>Tono cercano, profesional, comunitario. Plural inclusivo ("nosotros", "la comunidad").</li>
        <li>Voz activa. Tutea o usa "ustedes" según la audiencia, pero sé consistente dentro de cada página.</li>
        <li>Evita anglicismos cuando exista un equivalente claro ("ponente" en lugar de "speaker" si se entiende mejor); úsalos cuando son convención técnica ("front-end", "DevOps").</li>
        <li>Un signo de admiración por página máximo. Punto.</li>
        <li>Números: del uno al nueve en letra; del 10 en adelante en dígitos. Siempre dígitos para fechas y métricas.</li>
        <li>Comillas latinas en prosa larga; comillas dobles rectas en código y UI técnica.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">
        <table class="min-w-full text-sm">
          <thead class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800">
            <tr class="text-left">
              <th class="px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">Sí</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">No</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-200 dark:divide-gray-700">
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">"Pereira Tech Talks organiza meetups mensuales en Pereira desde 2017."</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">"Somos el ecosistema de innovación más vanguardista de la región."</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">"Postula como ponente y comparte lo que aprendiste."</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">"¡Postula ya — cupos limitados!"</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">"Los patrocinadores reciben logo, lightning talk y un año de alianza."</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">"Beneficios premium incomparables al mejor valor."</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">"Nos reunimos cada viernes durante la cuarentena — 130+ charlas."</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">"Una travesía de innovación que redefine los límites."</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Hard rule — orthography</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
        Spanish content always uses ñ (<code>pequeño</code>, <code>diseño</code>,
        <code>español</code>), accented vowels (<code>análisis</code>, <code>código</code>,
        <code>página</code>, <code>versión</code>), and interrogative accents
        (<code>cómo</code>, <code>qué</code>, <code>cuál</code>). The greps in
        <code>AGENTS.md</code> §2 must return zero matches before commit.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Forbidden vocabulary</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
        Replace these on sight. Full list in
        <code>docs/WRITING_VOICE_GUIDE.md</code>:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 space-y-1">
        <li>"leverage", "synergy", "ecosystem-as-a-service", "revolutionary", "best-in-class"</li>
        <li>"vanguardista", "disruptivo", "ecosistema de innovación", "líder del mercado"</li>
        <li>Stacked exclamation marks, ALL-CAPS sentences, emojis in chrome</li>
        <li>"Don't miss out", "Hurry", "Limited time" — we don't sell scarcity</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">Names &amp; conventions</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 space-y-1">
        <li><strong>Pereira Tech Talks</strong> — full name, title case. <strong>PTT</strong> in compact UI / chrome.</li>
        <li><strong>Pereira Tech Day {`{year}`}</strong> — full name, title case. <strong>PTD {`{year}`}</strong> in compact UI.</li>
        <li><strong>La Biblioteca del Mañana</strong> — proper noun in both languages; never translate.</li>
        <li><strong>Speaker School</strong> — proper noun; in Spanish use "Speaker School" too (consolidated brand).</li>
        <li>Locations: "Pereira, Risaralda, Colombia" — full string only on first mention or in metadata.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
</InternalLayout>
